  "description": "Introducing the Thorn Mercury 40 Celebrating 40 Years of Thorn Innovation The Mercury 40 is our all-new, high-performance touring and sportive bike – launched to mark Thorn’s 40th anniversary. It replaces the Club Tour Mk5, Mercury Mk3 Rohloff, and the Audax drop-bar bike, combining the best features of each into one versatile, responsive machine. Designed for Performance & Versatility Built from Thorn 858 seamless, double-butted, heat-treated Cro-Mo steel, the Mercury 40 is engineered for a lively, comfortable ride – whether you’re chasing miles on a lightweight setup or loading up for long-haul touring. Compatible with 700c & 650B wheels Belt-drive ready with a frame gate Choice of forks: Carbon disc or lightweight 853 steel Brake options: Disc or V-brake mounts Tyre clearance: 700c: up to 40mm (38mm with mudguards) 650B: up to 50mm (with or without mudguards) Custom Fit Options The Mercury 40 comes in 8 frame sizes to suit most riders: 5 sizes with long top tubes – ideal for flat bars 3 sizes with short top tubes – perfect for drop bars or a more relaxed flat bar setup New steel fork option offers more clearance (up to 44mm with mudguards), giving you greater flexibility in how you build your Mercury. Features at a Glance High-quality Thorn 858 steel tubing (from our Audax Mk4) Lightweight, sporty geometry for a faster, more responsive ride Mounts for three bottles, a stand plate under the bottom bracket, and full touring gear Built for Rohloff or derailleur gearing Chain or belt drive compatible Colour Options Frame: Metallic Gunmetal or Metallic Orange Forks: Black (both carbon and steel - see associated products below) Who Is It For? Whether you're upgrading from a Nomad Mk3 or looking for a bike that blends speed, comfort, and capability, the Mercury 40 is designed to handle it all — from fast club rides to multi-day touring. One bike. Endless possibilities. If unsure of size please contact Thorn on 01278 441505, Monday to Thursday from 8.00am to 4.00pm or sales@thorncycles.co.uk. Please note that we no longer have an open showroom.",
